This directory contains the Beginner-level projects completed as part of the CyberSNova Blue Team Cybersecurity Internship.

The projects focus on developing foundational Blue Team skills through practical security investigations, log analysis, SIEM monitoring, phishing detection, and Windows event log analysis.

Projects

1. Linux System Log Analysis

Analyzing Linux and SSH logs to identify suspicious authentication activity, brute-force attempts, failed logins, and anomalous events.

2. Email Header Analysis & Phishing Triage

Investigating phishing email samples by examining SPF, DKIM, DMARC authentication results, email headers, and suspicious indicators.

3. Building a Home SOC – SIEM Setup & Log Ingestion

Setting up a Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) environment using Wazuh or Splunk, ingesting sample logs, and creating dashboards to monitor failed login attempts.

4. Windows Event Log Fundamentals

Investigating Windows Event Logs to identify successful and failed logon events, analyze relevant Event IDs, and understand suspicious authentication activity.

